{
  "case_id": "2006-06-618",
  "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: JEAN M. MANNING, ESQ., Senate Chief Counsel for employment, Washington D.C.; on behalf of Appellant. RICHARD A. SALZMAN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Appellee. THOMAS E. CABALLERO, ESQ., Assistant Senate Legal Counsel, Washington, D.C.; for United States Senate, as amicus curiae, supporting Appellee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Do you think -- do you think that we owe any special measure of respect to the Congress, that is most intimately concerned with the Speech or Debate Clause, with their view that this is, this legislation is compatible with that clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And in we recite that the district court held the Act unconstitutional as applied to appellees and dismissed the charges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What's wrong with this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Isn't that a -- can you give me examples of cases where that Act applies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Can you give me instances in which employees of an the office of a Senator are covered by these obligations and cannot invoke the Speech or Debate Clause? What's the classic example where you can't invoke the Speech or Debate Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If this statute was set up so that the defendant here was the Senate, as opposed to the office of a Senator, would you still say that this suit couldn't go forward?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well why doesn't it matter who the defendant is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: And how do we do it? I mean, you've said -- I don't want to go too far with a metaphor, but you spoke a moment ago of there being sort of a, what did you say, a hole or a space in the legislative sphere when somebody is fired."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why isn't it a waiver of sovereign immunity when you set up a suit that envisions a suit which will be paid off by the Senate? Why isn't that a waiver of sovereign immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: What if his dissent -- or defense, rather, to the charge is that he was very inefficient in giving me help in legislative hearings and so forth, or words of that kind which might be arguably a legislative act, and that Speech or Debate Clause forbids inquiry into the quality of his performing those duties?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: What's the test for intruding? If it would chill his exercise of the function in future cases, or if it requires him to talk about legislative decisions, or what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Yes, but what if the Senator doesn't want to put it in? I mean, what if he does not want to waive the privilege? Is his only choice in effect to sit moot and lose the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Salzman",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALZMAN: Well, in Brewster, Your Honor, this Court recognized that there may be situations where the court permits an indictment to go forward, in which the indictment itself and the proof that the prosecutor will be presenting does not so intrude on the legislative process that it would be precluded but that the Defendant may decide that in order to explain the accusation he needs to rely on legislative acts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I have one question. The Appellants here were the ones that appealed to the court of appeals? Did they appeal from the district court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Senate",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF THOMAS E. CABALLERO ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES SENATE AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING APPELLEE MR. CABALLERO: Justice Stevens and may it please the Court: We agree that there is no jurisdiction in this Court under Section 412. But I first would like to correct one of the answers regarding cases under this Congressional Accountability Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "which the Court has found that jurisdiction is barred in Speech or Debate Clause cases. The first is when the case is predicated on a legislative act. The second is when the case cannot, that is cannot be adjudicated without questioning a legislative act or the motive for the act. And the third is when the member will be made to answer in terms of his defense for a legislative act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Right. I have one -- one question. Could the Senate direct you to pay this judgment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Manning",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MANNING: They cannot direct us to pay. It of course comes out of the Treasury fund and the Senate has had absolutely no control or involvement at all for 12 years in any of these cases. They do not know --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could it, if it chose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-618",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 2:02 p.m., the case in the above-titled matter was submitted.)"
    },
